Use the C-array names for MuPDF's embedded fonts (_binary_<name>) on any
musl target. Zig-built MuPDF uses them on x86_64 as on ARM; Plato assumes
the ld -b binary names (_binary_resources_fonts_..._start) on x86 Linux.

